WEBVTT

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.300
Gotansha Publishing

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.830
Weekly JIDAI Magazine
Over 600,000 Copies Printed

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.800
On Sale Every Monday

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.330
This picture has already been
through a quality check, right?

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.050
Pick up the damn phone!

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.210
I personally think it's ready for print as-is.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.420
I see. So you're not willing to rewrite it.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:29.590
Matsukata!

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.410
Take care of this.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.130
Narita-san.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.960
Just because it's good enough for you
doesn't mean it gets an okay from me.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:35.750
Shinji

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.790
Hey, Matsukata! About Tanaka's article...

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.050
No way!

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:04.170
Shigoto dekiru otoko sore ga kanojo no konomi
A man who can work, that's the type she likes

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.460
Kiai irete tsutometa no daga
I psyched myself up and got down to business

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.040
Isogashii wa tsuman nai wa
But I'm always so busy and so bored

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.710
Ima no kaisha kanari level takai hou dashi
The company I work at now is pretty high level

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.880
Oyaji garami no kone mo aru kara
And my dad has a lot of connections there

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.040
Yameru wakya nai shi
So there's no way I can quit

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:40.460
Itsumo boku wa hitori kiri
I'm always all by myself

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:45.630
Furo ni haitte neru dake
I just take a bath and fall asleep

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:51.040
Nagameru koto sae dekinai
I can't even take the time to admire

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:57.500
Kimi no kami o aruku sugata o
Your hair or the way you walk

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:02.800
Nerukoto shika dekinai
If all I can do is sleep

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:09.050
Semete yume no naka de demo
Then at least in my dreams

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:11.080
Kimi ni aitai
I want to see you

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:17.920
The Female Hataraki Man

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.960
Matsukata-san, thanks for your help today.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:29.960
Honestly, I didn't think it was necessary,
but you had to rewrite my article in the end.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.670
However, next time I'll take care of it on my own.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.050
So no matter what the boss says,
please don't get involved.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:42.540
Hiroko Matsukata (28)
Occupation: Magazine Editor

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.500
To be frank, this job is really tedious.
I've thought about quitting many times.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.540
Usually just before I proofread something.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.170
Used to have a bigger chest
Or when a stupid newbie gets totally full of himself.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.510
Oh, she's asleep.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:48.630
Tanaka.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.380
The editor-in-chief wants you
to come drinking tonight.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:59.870
Kunio Tanaka (22)
Newly Hired Editor

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.000
Going out with everybody from
the office after work... That's not my scene.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.830
I'd prefer not to get lectured while I drink.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.170
I'm sorry, I have plans tonight.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:03.210
Oh, I see.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.340
I'm leaving for the day.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.340
Don't invite that jerk!

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.340
Matsukata-senpai, you were awake this whole time?

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:15.410
My brain shut down to avoid hearing
whatever he had to say.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.460
Tanaka... Maybe I screwed up by letting him go
to the reference room during the final stretch.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.090
Then he didn't even watch us handle
the most crucial part.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.540
He was in the way, so I just sent him off.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.840
After having his work sent back for revision
so many times, how can he be so arrogant?

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.540
Get down in the dirt and work!

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:34.750
I was so inspired today!
Matsukata-senpai is a real Hataraki Man!

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.710
A "Hataraki Man," that's fitting.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:40.380
Why exactly am I a "man"?

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.540
Matsukata... that's because you're so manly.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.420
Kaji-san, hearing that from you
makes it feel like a compliment.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:54.250
Kimio Narita (39)
Senior Editor of Weekly JIDAI

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:51.710
I think among our younger staff,
the women have more energy than the men.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.250
But I hear that's the same in most other workplaces.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.340
Huh? Where did Matsukata go?

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.460
She said she had a date tonight and left.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.340
A date? I bet her partner is a woman.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:12.630
Tatsuhiko Umemiya (45)
Editor-in-Chief of Weekly JIDAI

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.260
These days if you're not careful
and just shoot your mouth off,

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:12.500
they'll come at you with claims of sexual
or power harassment. Better to just stop talking.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.790
But yeah, Matsukata is a "Hataraki Man" for sure.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.210
She's already gotten approval for her
next three articles.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.540
What's wrong, Mayu-chan?

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.670
None of my pitches for articles got approved.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:35.920
Mayu Nagisa (23)
Occupation: Magazine Editor

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.290
I was told the articles I wanted
to write weren't good enough.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:35.420
But unless I write about something
I'm interested in, I can't get serious about it!

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.580
Jeez... how does that girl find time to sleep?

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.420
Oh, I almost forgot. I got a text from Shinji.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:50.840
Shinji
Sorry!!
Sorry! Something came up
at work, so I can't make
it tonight. I'll call you later.
-Shinji

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.380
Sorry! Something came up at work,
so I can't make it tonight. I'll call you later. Shinji.

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:54.630
What a relief... I'm too exhausted for a date.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.580
Now I can get some sleep.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:57.920
Keep it up,

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:58.800
Keep it up, do your best.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:01.540
Keep it up, do your best.
-Hiro ♥

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.330
That reply should make him happy.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.090
I'm too exhausted to even talk right now.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.710
We haven't had sex in over 3 months...

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.670
I worked myself ragged and now
I don't know what I want to do...

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.040
My makeup... Should wash it off...

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:27.370
It's too late... I don't care... anymore...

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:34.000
Oh, that pitch of yours "The Glamorous Lifestyle
of our Foreign Affairs Minister," was approved.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.380
Ah, okay. I'm already working on it.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.290
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.170
We were supposed to start at 8,
and it's already 7 minutes past!

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:49.800
Originally we scheduled 30 minutes for this,

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:53.370
but his plans afterwards have changed,
so you'll only have 15.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.370
Huh? B-but that means there
are only 8 minutes left now!

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.830
The Minister tires easily.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.500
Who changes their plans so suddenly
this late at night?!

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.010
I can't believe I bothered to get dressed up for this.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.870
Oh shit! Did they hear me?

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.090
You must be the reporter.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.170
How strange, I wonder why they're making you wait.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:18.550
Hold on a second.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:23.920
It's okay to come in now.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.250
Thank you very much.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.710
Weekly JIDAI? But you're not Kaji-san.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:30.840
I thought this interview would be with her.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:34.210
Sorry about that.
Could I ask you some questions now?

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.880
Uh, what was this about again?

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:38.630
The article is going to highlight
your glamorous lifestyle.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:40.130
Ah, glamorous, I see.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.090
Some may consider the life of a politician glamorous,
but we work on behalf of the people, so...

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.790
Those are some thick fingers.
Some may consider the life of a politician glamorous,
but we work on behalf of the people, so...

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:45.790
He must grab a lot of stuff with those.
Some may consider the life of a politician glamorous,
but we work on behalf of the people, so...

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.130
Thank you very much.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:54.090
Lastly, I'd like to ask:
What does your job mean to you, Minister?

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:57.130
Please submit your article by tomorrow.
We'll need to check it.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.290
Minister!

00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.250
It's pointless.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:02.710
Oh, it's that shrewd woman from earlier.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.330
It's pointless to ask him a question like that.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:08.170
He has absolutely no sense of ideals or aesthetics.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:10.420
Um, excuse me, but...

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:16.380
His wife? No, lover.
Maybe the secretary-turned-mistress.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:18.790
In any case, she looks pretty heartless.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.290
I just can't get motivated.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.460
How do I turn this into a good article?

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.420
You made the pitch for it yourself, right?

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:31.170
Mayu-kun, articles you want to write are different
from the articles that actually get accepted.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.410
Oh... I get it.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:37.010
He has absolutely no sense of ideals or aesthetics.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.500
I might have had those when I started this job.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:43.580
Something similar to ideals...
and a sense of aesthetics...

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:47.880
Hello?

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.800
Hey, Hiro! Sorry about the other day.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.120
I'm downstairs right now,
let's grab something to eat.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:54.380
Now?

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.960
Wait just a minute.

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:00.670
Hello, you've reached the offices of Weekly JIDAI.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:04.040
May I speak to the reporter
who interviewed the Foreign Affairs Minister?

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:05.500
It's that woman!

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.580
Y-you're speaking to her...

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.380
I have something to discuss with you.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.090
Regarding the Minister.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.130
A leak from the inside.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.920
Oh my God, this could be huge!

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.160
Yes.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.130
Sorry Shinji, I can't right now.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.550
I'm really sorry, some other time!

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.620
Do you always put work above all else?

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:35.000
I'm not trying to act cool or stand out
by choosing work over play... jerk.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.000
Right now, none of that matters.

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:39.710
I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:41.630
That was fast.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:43.330
Of course.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.830
Shall we begin?

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:48.630
G'morning.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:49.510
Boss!

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.880
What? Did you stay overnight in the office again?

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:54.080
I just finished gathering the details on a big story.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.460
The Foreign Affairs Minister, Hikaru Hoshikawa,
has been misappropriating public funds.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.250
I have data and testimony
from someone directly involved.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:02.750
Wait here for a minute.

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:04.630
Umemiya-san.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:13.040
Matsukata!

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.250
Update the cover of this issue!

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:18.750
The best feeling in the world is the moment
when all your hard work pays off.

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:22.960
Add the title "Foreign Affairs Minister
Hikaru Hoshikawa Betrays His Country"!

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.750
The article goes straight to page 8!

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:25.920
Yessir!

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.330
Work mode, on!

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.080
Manly switch...

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:30.290
HIYAA!

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.630
Activate!

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:34.960
There she is! The Hataraki Man!

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.870
Hey, is it okay to put this data on page 2?

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:39.500
No, it's out of date.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.330
For a senior editor, you sure are useless.

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:43.000
Allow me to explain.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.040
When she becomes Hataraki Man,
the male hormones in her blood multiply,

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.330
When she becomes Hataraki Man,
the male hormones in her blood multiply,
Is the layout finished? There's only 3 hours left to print!

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:49.300
enabling her to work at a speed
three times faster than normal.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:53.840
During this period, any notion of sleep, food,
love, clothing, and hygiene completely vanishes!

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.550
Well, I'm done for today.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.420
Alleged Abuse of Secret Funds

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.710
Foreign Affairs Minister Hikaru
Hoshikawa Betrays His Country!

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:08.380
New Releases

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.000
Narita-san!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.330
Hm? What?

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:16.460
There's a call for Matsukata-senpai,
but the person on the other end is scaring me...

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:17.540
Where is Matsukata?

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.170
She hasn't come in yet.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.340
Then just hang up on them.

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:21.540
Huh?! But...

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:22.580
It's fine, it's fine.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:26.000
We decided that she has
to handle all of those calls herself.

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:30.130
I see. So, she has to be here to take the call.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:31.460
Good morning!

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.590
I feel sick...

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.710
Did you run all the way here again?

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:40.380
How... did you know?

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:44.290
You're the type that will rush onto
a leaving train even though you aren't late.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:47.500
It's a conditional reflex you have
when you hear the departure chime.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:52.080
By the way, I want you
to assist Tanaka on his article.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.250
Ah, I'm okay.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:58.000
I'm gathering opinions online
and checking my work against some older articles.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.750
I think it will meet your standards.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.540
Oh? Are you sure about that?

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:07.080
Well, I'm enjoying doing it my way
at a pace that's comfortable.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:12.960
When I see guys like him, I start to question myself.

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:18.370
Working my ass off on "pitches that get approved"
and "articles that readers will enjoy"...

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.370
No, it's better this way.

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:22.840
In response to the news, Minister Hoshikawa
has claimed that one of his secretaries,

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:25.000
Under Suspicion
Minister Hikaru Hoshikawa's
